course: dictionary
lesson: 8227
title: Changing back
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Reversible means able to be changed back to how it was before. When you meet a new word, look at the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues. «Melting, freezing, boiling and condensing are reversible changes, because the molecules stay the same.»
explain: The clues are «changes» and «stay the same». A change that can be undone is one where the stuff goes back to how it was. Melting ice makes water, and freezing that water makes ice again, so the change is reversible.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Melting, freezing, boiling and condensing are able to be changed back, because the molecules stay the same.» It still makes sense, so reversible means able to be changed back.
fact: Reversible means able to be changed back to how it was before.
fact: A reversible change in science is one where you can get the original materials back, like melting ice or dissolving salt.
fact: «Reversible» also describes clothes that can be worn either side out, like a «reversible jacket».
fact: In maths, adding is reversed by subtracting, so the two operations undo each other.
fact: Burning wood and cooking an egg are not reversible: you cannot get the original materials back.
exercise: «Melting, freezing, boiling and condensing are reversible changes.» What does reversible mean here? | Hard to melt | Able to be seen through | *Able to be changed back to how it was before | Very quick to happen
exercise: A «reversible jacket» can be worn how? | *Either side out | Without arms | Upside down only | Only in the rain
exercise: Which of these is a reversible change? | Cooking an egg | Rusting a nail | *Melting ice | Burning a candle
test: Which of these is a reversible change? | Cooking an egg | Rusting iron | *Dissolving salt in water | Burning wood
test: Which of these describes a reversible jacket? | Worn only on Sundays | *Able to be worn either side out | Ripped at the hem | Made of paper
exam: Which word means a change where the original materials can be got back? | *Reversible | Burning | Irreversible | Rusting
